    "id": "train-2425",
    "question": "Mabel has 5 daisies in her garden, and each daisy has 8 petals.  If she gives 2 daisies to her teacher, how many petals does she have on the remaining daisies in her garden?",
    "gold": "24",
    "answer": "The total number of petals Mabel has in her garden is 5 x 8 = <<5*8=40>>40 petals.\nThe total number of petals that Mabel gives to her teacher is 2 x 8 = <<2*8=16>>16 petals.\nThe total number of petals remaining in her garden is 40 - 16 = <<40-16=24>>24 petals.\n#### 24"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many petals Mabel has on the remaining daisies in her garden, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of petals on all the daisies initially in the garden.\n2. Determine the number of daisies Mabel has after giving some to her teacher.\n3. Calculate the total number of petals on the remaining daisies.\n\nStep 1: Calculate the total number of petals on all the daisies initially in the garden.\nMabel has 5 daisies, and each daisy has 8 petals.\n\\[\n5 \\text{ daisies} \\times 8 \\text{ petals per daisy} = 40 \\text{ petals}\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Determine the number of daisies Mabel has after giving some to her teacher.\nMabel gives 2 daisies to her teacher, so she has:\n\\[\n5 \\text{ daisies} - 2 \\text{ daisies} = 3 \\text{ daisies}\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Calculate the total number of petals on the remaining daisies.\nEach of the remaining 3 daisies has 8 petals.\n\\[\n3 \\text{ daisies} \\times 8 \\text{ petals per daisy} = 24 \\text{ petals}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of petals on the remaining daisies in Mabel's garden is \\(\\boxed{24}\\).",
